{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794129629,"nonce":"QtSis3yFC11OFkmIu1B++TxCJa4=","message":"Correction to the description. The Linux theme's sans family is Cantarell with fallbacks Ubuntu, DejaVu Sans, system-ui, sans-serif (the Ubuntu-first list is the generic system_sans stack's fallback tail). blinc_text's Linux registry list is Cantarell, Ubuntu, Noto Sans, DejaVu Sans. So the two lists disagree on Noto Sans, and neither starts with Ubuntu. The reporter's claim that fontconfig substitutes a missing family is unverified: the registry queries fontdb by name and may not use fontconfig at all. To settle: measure a named missing family and see what it resolves to (the NUC has Ubuntu and Noto Sans, not Cantarell, so Cantarell is a missing-first-family case there). Nothing changed yet.","files":null}]}